abstract: >-
  DoseCurve is a free, browser-based simulator for teaching pharmacokinetics and PK/PD.
  It models one- and two-compartment kinetics (first-order or saturable Michaelis-Menten) for
  oral, IV bolus and infusion dosing with regular, loading, missed and custom schedules; a clinical
  patient with Cockcroft-Gault creatinine clearance; hemodialysis, a liver model, antimicrobial
  PK/PD indices, effect-site delays and indirect responses; population variability; and Bayesian
  individualization from measured levels. It has a cited drug library, guided lessons, generated
  practice problems, clinical cases graded by the model, and a public validation against an
  independent solver. It is an educational model, not for clinical dosing.
